Privacy Policy for EPOD Mobile App
Effective Date: January 14, 2026
1. Introduction
EPOD Mobile App (“EPOD”) is an Electronic Proof of Delivery (EPOD) application developed by Tridex Systems and integrated with an organization’s Infor CloudSuite environment.
The App is intended solely for authorized employees of organizations that deploy EPOD. It enables delivery drivers to manage deliveries, view customer information, collect proof of delivery, capture images, and continue working while offline.
This Privacy Policy explains what information EPOD collects, how it is used, where it is stored, and how it is protected.
________________________________________
2. Information We Collect
EPOD collects and processes only the information necessary to perform proof-of-delivery operations.
Employee Information
•	Name
•	Company email address
•	Organization or company information
Delivery Information
The App may process:
•	Customer delivery addresses
•	Customer phone numbers (to allow drivers to contact customers regarding deliveries)
•	Delivery order information
•	Customer signatures collected as proof of delivery
•	Delivery photographs
•	Delivery notes entered by drivers
Device & Diagnostic Information
EPOD may collect limited device and application diagnostic information, including:
•	Device information required for troubleshooting
•	Application error logs
•	Diagnostic information generated by the Infor Mongoose platform
In certain error scenarios, diagnostic logs may contain delivery-related information necessary to investigate and resolve application issues.
________________________________________
3. Authentication
Users authenticate using their organization’s Microsoft Single Sign-On (SSO) through Infor CloudSuite.
EPOD does not create independent user accounts and does not store user passwords.
________________________________________
4. Permissions Used
EPOD requests only the permissions required to provide its functionality.
Camera
Used to:
•	Capture proof-of-delivery photographs
•	Scan Infor ION API QR codes
Photos / Storage
Used to:
•	Upload delivery photographs
•	Access images selected by the user for delivery records
Phone
Used to:
•	Allow drivers to call customers directly regarding deliveries
EPOD does not collect or track the device’s GPS location.
________________________________________
5. How Information Is Stored
EPOD does not store delivery or user information on servers owned or operated by Tridex Systems.
Instead:
•	All delivery information is stored within the customer’s Infor CloudSuite environment.
•	Diagnostic logs are stored within the customer’s Infor Mongoose environment.
•	Offline delivery data is securely stored on the device until network connectivity is available, after which it is synchronized with the customer’s Infor CloudSuite tenant using encrypted connections.
Developers do not independently copy, export, or maintain customer delivery data.
________________________________________
6. How Information Is Used
Information processed by EPOD is used solely to:
•	Authenticate authorized users
•	Display assigned deliveries
•	Record proof of delivery
•	Capture customer signatures and photographs
•	Allow drivers to contact customers regarding deliveries
•	Synchronize offline delivery information
•	Troubleshoot application issues
•	Maintain and improve application reliability
________________________________________
7. Data Sharing
EPOD does not sell or share personal information with advertisers or unrelated third parties.
Information collected through the App is available only to:
•	The customer organization that owns and manages the Infor CloudSuite tenant
•	Authorized support personnel, when granted access by the customer for troubleshooting purposes
Developer access to customer data is available only through customer-provided accounts and solely for support and maintenance activities.
________________________________________
8. Analytics and Diagnostics
EPOD uses the diagnostic capabilities provided by the Infor Mongoose platform to record application errors and assist with troubleshooting.
EPOD does not use third-party analytics, advertising, or marketing services such as Firebase Analytics.
Diagnostic information is used only to support, maintain, and improve the application’s reliability and performance.
________________________________________
9. Security
EPOD communicates with Infor CloudSuite using secure encrypted connections.
Offline data stored on the device is encrypted until it is synchronized.
Access to customer data and diagnostic logs is controlled by the customer’s Infor CloudSuite and Infor Mongoose security permissions.
While reasonable technical and organizational safeguards are implemented, no method of electronic storage or transmission can be guaranteed to be completely secure.
________________________________________
10. Third-Party Services
EPOD integrates with:
•	Microsoft authentication services for user sign-in
•	Infor CloudSuite APIs
•	Infor Mongoose platform services
No advertising networks or unrelated third-party services receive delivery information collected by the App.
________________________________________
11. Children’s Privacy
EPOD is intended solely for authorized employees of customer organizations.
The App is not directed toward children under the age of 13, and Tridex Systems does not knowingly collect personal information from children.
